# One-student lesson format

- Every lesson is taught to exactly one student by one teacher.
- Never copy group-work instructions from source screenshots literally.
- Rewrite `Work in pairs`, `Ask your partner`, `Work in groups`, and similar directions for one student.
- Prefer concrete instructions such as:
  - `Ask your teacher and answer the questions.`
  - `Read the questions aloud and answer them.`
  - `Discuss the questions with your teacher.`
  - `Take turns with your teacher.`
- Keep references to friends or other people when they are part of a dialogue, story, or grammar example rather than a classroom grouping instruction.
